-- title:
--   Branch-adapted crossing presentation of a completed local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative noetherian local ring and let $\widehat R$ denote its completion with respect to the maximal ideal of $R$. Let $W$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete with respect to its maximal ideal, let $\pi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $E$ be a natural number with $1 \le E$. Let $\theta \colon W[\![X_0,X_1]\!] \to \widehat R$ be a surjective ring homomorphism from the power series ring in two variables over $W$, let $v$ be a unit of $\widehat R$, and assume the relation $\theta(X_0)\,\theta(X_1) = \theta(C\pi)^E \cdot v$, where $C$ denotes the constant-coefficient inclusion $W \to W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$, together with $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} \widehat R \ge 2$. Then there exists a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from $\widehat R$ onto `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ E)`, that is onto the quotient of $W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(\pi^E)$, such that $\iota(\theta(C o))$ is the class `const (π ^ E) o` of $C o$ for every $o \in W$, that $\iota(\theta(X_0)) =$ `U (π ^ E)` $\cdot\, \iota(v)$, and that $\iota(\theta(X_1)) =$ `V (π ^ E)`, where `U (π ^ E)` and `V (π ^ E)` are the two distinguished coordinate elements of the crossing model.
--
--   This is the crossing (ordinary double point of thickness $E$, i.e. $A_{E-1}$) presentation of a two-dimensional completed local ring, in a form in which the isomorphism is pinned on the chosen generators: the coordinates $\theta(X_0)$, $\theta(X_1)$ are matched with $U$ and $V$ up to the given unit, so that the two branch ideals can be transported along $\iota$. It is used for the local description of nodal curves and their moduli, being cited by the local-chart analyses of crossing schemes, node annuli and Drinfeld-type curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_of_mul_eq_pow_mul_unit.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open ModularCurve ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel

theorem IsLocalRing.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_of_mul_eq_pow_mul_unit
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    {W : Type*} [CommRing W] [IsDomain W] [IsDiscreteValuationRing W]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal W) W]
    (π : W) (hπ : Irreducible π) (E : ℕ) (hE : 1 ≤ E)
    (θ : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W →+* AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R)
    (hθ : Function.Surjective θ)
    (v : (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R)ˣ)
    (hrel : θ (MvPowerSeries.X 0) * θ (MvPowerSeries.X 1) =
      θ (MvPowerSeries.C π) ^ E * (v : AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R))
    (hdim : 2 ≤ ringKrullDim (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R)) :
    ∃ ι : AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R ≃+* UVCrossingModel W (π ^ E),
      (∀ o : W, ι (θ (MvPowerSeries.C o)) = const (π ^ E) o) ∧
      ι (θ (MvPowerSeries.X 0)) = U (π ^ E) * ι (v : AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R) ∧
      ι (θ (MvPowerSeries.X 1)) = V (π ^ E) := by sorry
